# I plan my day and week using time-blocking method. I use cron to enforce my
# time block boundaries and breaks as most of my work is being done on PC and
# phone (I use sth. similar on my phone).
#
# Advantages as opposed to only using alarms on phone:
#   1. I don't have to think about my schedule and manage alarms.
#   2. Alarms may go unnoticed (e.g. if my phone is in a different room or out
#   of battery).
#   3. There is no postpone button. I don't waste my willpower to keep my
#   time-blocks sharp.
#   4. I can always leave my PC on when I go away (it will turn off itself
#   eventually).
#   5. Easier context switches between morning and evening time blocks and
#   cleaner PC desktop.
#   6. It is less likely that my attention gets stolen/grabbed by a low
#   priority engaging or urgent task as the time-block boundary/break helps me
#   to reevaluate my priorities for the day resp. "unfocus", so that I am able
#   to do a calm prioritization.
#
# Disadvantages of managing my daily schedule this way:
#   1. ONLINE CALLS need to fit time-block boundaries! Having my screen locked
#   or PC turned off in the middle of an online call is annoying, but this is
#   also a blessing in disguise as I am forced to schedule my online calls to
#   fit my time-blocks, not the other way around.
#
#   Note: shutdown command uses a default "+1m" delay, hence if I am caught off
#   guard, I can return by turning my PC on back again and 1m is just enough
#   time to finish what I was doing.


*      0-6    * * *  root /sbin/shutdown

# --- 7 - 9 Time block 0 (phone on for 10 min) ---

50-59   8      * * TUE,WED,FRI-SUN  root /usr/bin/loginctl lock-sessions

# --- 9 - 12 Time block 1 (phone off) ---

# --- Sext, lunch and walk (phone on) ---
# Locks session shortly before shutdown (gives a warning effect)
55     11     * * *  root /usr/bin/loginctl lock-sessions
*      12     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown

# --- 13 - 15 Time block 2 (phone off) ---
# 15,17  15     * * *  root /usr/bin/loginctl lock-sessions

# --- 15:30 - 17:40 Time block 3 (phone off) ---

# 17:40 - alarm on phone - supper

# --- 18:00 - 20:00 Bonus time block (optional, phone on)

# Locks session shortly before shutdown (gives a warning effect)
50,55  19     * * *  root /usr/bin/loginctl lock-sessions
*      20-23  * * *  root /sbin/shutdown


# === WEEKLY SCHEDULE ===
# Saturday
*      18-20  * * Sat  root /sbin/shutdown
# Sunday - rest/sport
*      12-20  * * Sun  root /sbin/shutdown

